{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/22416-campaign-ideas","id":22416,"title":"Campaign Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-03T10:38:30-08:00","id":22416,"title":"Campaign Ideas","content":"I'd like to hear everyone's ideas for campaigns. Even those that have already been used in games, but also some ones you'd like to try out.<br /> <br /> 1. A set of twin Scions of Loki, after conversing with each other and several other children of less-than-reputable gods, have come up with a foolproof plan to avoid Ragnarok and save their father: destiny says that Loki's slaying of Baldur trigger his final imprisonment and spring Ragnarok from near-certainty to Inevitable. In order to save Loki, they simply have to finish the series of oaths to make baldur invincible, while distracting Loki from the process. But as the pair of tricksters wheel and deal their way through the world, the strands of Fate begin to tighten around Loki; the closer Baldur comes to absolute invincibility, the more furious and malignant Loki seems to become. Can the Lord of Lies truly be distracted/held in check long enough for the pair to finish the job, or will their good intentions cause the downfall of their father, and the Norse Pantheon itself?<br /> <br /> 2. Aphrodite has fallen for the god of war.... Hachiman. And try as he might, the attentions of the Greek goddess of love are starting to seep into Hachiman's brain an heart as well. Yet, as you can imagine, both Zeus and Amaterasu seem to be against this long-distance relationship, for who knows what sort of godling will come from a meeting of Kami and Theoi. Aphrodite and Hachiman are looking for someplace to elope, and have come to the Scion party to help their search for a place 'where neither sun nor lightning can find them' before the vow is complete, promising a wealth of tomes and Birthrights to whoever protects them until the child can be born. Can anyone convince the two lovebirds to call it off, and who in their right mind would want this union to come to fruition? And can anyone convince Hephaestus to not build giant, rampaging automatons to find and punish the ill-suited duo?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T10:59:37-08:00","id":22444,"title":"","content":"This occurred in our home-game at god-level:<br /> <br /> A scion of Loki, fed up with the forced association with his father and pissed about his status in the Aesir came up with a plan to ensure Heimdall survives. To do this he enlisted the help of a Deev whose ambition outweighed his zealotry to the point where he sought to become a god in his won right and build his own pantheon (much trickery and skullduggery brought THAT about). This Deev seeded rumors of a way for that creature Tuisco from Ehekatoyaatl to replace Tyr entirely using the momentum from Ragnarok. Luring him onto the battlefield with assurances that his superior wind powers would allow him to buck Fate and take over. Tyr was distracted from battle with a series of bullshit attacks from air-monsters and abducted by this Deev while Tuisco replaced him. And replace him he did, for the ended up taking the doom of Tyr unto himself after renouncing the titanrealm to claim his &quot;prize&quot;. Thus we were down a nonsensical titan avatar and up a very confused Tyr, who then oversaw the duel between Loki and Heimdall, ensuring Loki could not kill him since ti was now a FAIR fight as per the Arbiter.<br /> <br /> My character, a Yazata, created a scheme exploiting the apparent fluidity of Ragnarok for our purposes by convincing that same scion of Loki to negotiate with his &quot;brother&quot; Jormungandr to stay out of the fight while we replaced him with Ahzi-Dahaka (which keeps him from rampaging across the world killing 1/3 it's population. We were having problems with the drowned road, so we convinced him (being that he's waaaay more powerful than the ruling avatars there) to go to The Drowned Road and TAKE OVER, along with Oceanus. An infinite sea would mean plenty of room for the world-serpent to swim, and having a titan-avatar in our pocket would help the new Aesir after the war (Win-Win situation!).<br /> <br /> Fenrir got replaced in a similar manner as Jormy did, and we got someone (a PC no less) to replace Hel in ruling Helheim, so she could roam at will and do what she wanted in return for her helping us frag the hell out of the titanarmies (which she did with relish, we kinda gave her Mazikeen's personality from Lucifer comics).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T12:02:44-08:00","id":22490,"title":"","content":"Here's some more.<br /> <br /> 3. The Pesedjet have grown quiet for an extended period of time, essentially leaving their Scions without guidance. In particular, Atem-Ra, Horus, and Set have become completely unreachable. This is eventually revealed to be a ploy by the three of them empower one particular Scion of Ra to unrivaled heights, as they systematically flood him with both Legend and the blood of titanspawn (generously donated by the Hummingbird of the South) in order to generate a Titan Avatar of Light. The party is then tasked to escort this Teotl-Pesedjet project into Akenaten, storm the gates of Aten, and replace him with the new, supposedly benign avatar. But have they taken things too far, and made a monster? Can you really trust a titan?<br /> -You can replace this with 'Light avatar comes to the Pesedjet and/or Aztlanti for aid in order to hide from Aten and gather power to himself, and Aten growing increasingly frantic in his search for him/her/it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T14:51:08-08:00","id":22609,"title":"","content":"Oh boy.... campaign ideas! I've got tons and tons. These ones are all Hero-level, and all in play at the moment so I can't actually broadcast more that the initial plothooks that started it all.<br /> <br /> 1.) It's 1570. The Scions wake up locked in stocks on a island that they don't know how long they've been there. Recruited by a slaver ship, they are forced to endlessly sail on a desolate sea and hunt down either ships that seem to come from various points in the past. Where they are, why they're there, and how long they've been there are only the beginning of their hunt for answers.<br /> <br /> 2.) New Orleans is the site of a strange three-way powerful truce between the Tuatha, the Yoruba, and the Teotl. Recently, unvisited Scions of each pantheon have begun disappearing and in order to prevent a political nuclear fallout, the answers need to be found out, and fast.<br /> <br /> 3.) Long ago, the Titans were sealed away by the Gods making a collective bargain with Order and Fate. In order to ensure that no Greater Titan could be freed, Legend was compressed and sealed away until no one thing was above Legend 4. One of these seals that has kept the world marginally in balance has been shattered and as the Gods are discovering; while they and their Scions might be trapped at Legend 4, the Titanspawn slipping through the cracks most certainly are not. Does the Band go on a quest to ensure the restructuring of the deal that first enclosed the Titans, or do they race against time to return Legend to the World proper before the Greater Titans become aware of the nasty loophole in their favor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T21:15:06-08:00","id":22883,"title":"","content":"An idea for a character and their subplot:<br /> -An idea I had for a character is an Amatsu-kami scion of Ama no Zako. He starts off believing he is serving the gods but is later revealed to be furthering titan interests. His big goal is to redeem his mother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T21:36:54-08:00","id":22893,"title":"","content":"It is the near future. The governments of the world have discovered Scions and are using them as a resource, and not in a good way. Scions with Epic Strength are being used as electrical generators or draft animals, et cetera et cetera. There are some level of artifact or whatever that lets Scions power be contained, while still allowing Scions to gain Legend to the point where they can sire more Scions to work for the State. The PCs are the Resistance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T14:08:45-08:00","id":34067,"title":"","content":"Recently newbie Scions have been lead into fatal ambushes, dozens across various pantheons have been claimed already. You and your circle are the only Scions to survive such attacks, because of this you're under suspcion of being in league with the conspirators! Your only chance is to find the real culprits and clear your name! Of course not every deity suspects you, including Baron Samedi and Hades who are willing to owe you a favor if you bring the conspirators to them, <i>alive</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T14:27:32-08:00","id":34078,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Titan War is raging, and the gods have been sending their latest, most powerful weapons at their ancient foes: Scions. However, the war is tough, things are getting tense, and many Scions fall to the Titanspawn. The Gods are scraping the bottom of the barrel at this point, Visiting every human who has even a drop of ichor, even those who are extremely aged or barely out of infancy, and preparing them for war. However, certain gods have connections to more than simply the human world. Many gods have taken totem animals, or are skilled shapeshifters, and those deities have produced children of a decidedly non-human nature. In the beginning of a divine experiment, a number of those gods have chosen to Visit their bestial offspring and make them Scions. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T12:49:52-08:00","id":34569,"title":"","content":"Well, my &quot;Scion High&quot; campaign worked out pretty well. Premise: You are Scions... in high school, dealing both with adolescent concerns while learning about the world of myth and Legend. Wackiness ensues. <br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T15:02:44-08:00","id":34624,"title":"","content":"As long as their ripping apart vampires..<br /> <br /> O wait, that's Buffy...<span style=\"font-size:9px\">who may have been a scion for a deity that hates parasites...</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T15:05:50-08:00","id":35156,"title":"","content":"The Titan War has ended. And with it begins the Divine Cold War. Pantheons are moving their pawns, arranging their forces against eachother, but no one's willing to take the first shot just yet. Caught in between this Mutually Assured Destruction scenario are you and your fellow Scions, who are almost assuredly coming from different Pantheons. Your parents are losing their patience. Will you join them and abandon the comrades you fought alongside with during the Titan War? Will you cut ties with your parents? Or even strike it out on your own? Do you have what it takes to convince your families to make peace with each other?<br /> <br /> What will you do Scion in the shadow of your parent's arms race?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T03:00:33-08:00","id":35481,"title":"","content":"A recent archeological dig uncovers a few relics and a long forgotten monster, whom for one reason or another you are called upon to deal with, the resalting ripple effect the long lost and newly released magics call forth more of their ilk. This continues on larger and larger scales until, finally the Gods of Old return...<br /> Flash forward 15 years, you play the children of your previous characters. This time you're Scions.<br /> <br /> What? With Origin I could totally do a campaign that runs like <i>Agents of Shield</i> and I could do the next campaign as <i>The Kane Chronicles</i>. (It did the 'sins of the father' thing better than percy Jackson.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}